# Cargo.lock is deliberately NOT ignored: this workspace ships binaries
# (rop-finder, rop-finder-mcp), so the exact resolved dependency set is part
# of the release artifact and of the parity numbers in docs/measured-2026-09.md.

# The tests/ harnesses (parity.py, doc_claims.py, chain_parity.py,
# mcp_workability.py) all `import rf_paths`, so running any gate leaves a
# tests/__pycache__ behind. It is build detritus, never an artifact.
__pycache__/

# Locally built release artifacts. Never committed: that is ENG-09, and
# dist/README.md explains why an unverifiable binary in git is worse than none.
dist/build/
dist/.zigshim/
